questions.question:
A die is rolled. Let A be the event 'a number greater than 2 appears' and B be the event 'an even number appears'. Match List-I with List-II.
List-I:
(a) A or B
(b) A and B
(c) A but not B
(d) not A
List-II:
(i) {3, 5}
(ii) {1, 2}
(iii) {4, 6}
(iv) {2, 3, 4, 5, 6}

Two dice are thrown and the sum of the numbers is noted. How many of the following collections of events form a set of mutually exclusive and exhaustive events?
(i) {sum is even, sum is odd}
(ii) {sum ≤ 6, sum ≥ 7}
(iii) {sum is prime, sum is a multiple of 2}
(iv) {sum < 5, 5 ≤ sum ≤ 8, sum > 8}
(v) {a doublet appears, sum is odd, sum is even but not a doublet}
(vi) {sum is a multiple of 3, sum is a multiple of 4, sum is a multiple of neither 3 nor 4}
